# the screen mirrored to a computer over USB (fm1.toml mirror = true: fm1-base's device/mirror.c, the site's Mirror
# page): a viewer's picture is the screen, pixel for pixel (tests/host/mirror_check.py, run_tests.sh), on a fast link
# and on one so slow that frames are dropped: once the link keeps up again, GIO-1 has drawn everything again
# (app_redraw) and the picture is whole
intro off
wait 1000
mirror out:stream.syx
wait 1500
tap ENV
wait 500
tap FX
wait 500
tap HOME
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 1500
fbdump fb.raw
mirror off
wait 200
tap PLAY
mirror_rate 2
mirror out:slow.syx
wait 1500
tap EDIT
wait 300
tap SEQ
wait 300
tap PLAY
wait 4000
# the link back to USB's pace: what was dropped is drawn again, and the viewer's picture is whole
mirror_rate 48
wait 1500
fbdump fb_slow.raw
mirror off
# GLO three times: the Mirror page. KNOB 1 Off: a computer's session gets no picture (tests/host/mirror_check.py
# --none), and it stays off after a restart; On again: mirrored again
mirror_rate 48
tap GLO
tap GLO
tap GLO
expect view 15
shot mirrorpage.png
turn K1 -1
expect mirror 0
tap SAVE
wait 300
reboot
wait 500
expect mirror 0
mirror out:off.syx
wait 1500
tap ENV
wait 500
mirror off
tap GLO
tap GLO
tap GLO
turn K1 1
expect mirror 1
mirror out:on.syx
wait 1500
fbdump fb_on.raw
mirror off
